(3499791, 488274, 70, '<td valign="top">This is neat because I just saw an exhibit at the local Institute of Arts called San Francisco Psychedelic. One whole room was posters from the Avalon and the Fillmore - a lot for the eyes to process! Nice setup. I''m not sure I''m crazy about the border here but I suppose it fits in quite well. (Not voting, just passing through. :) )</td>', 'This is neat because I just saw an exhibit at the local Institute of Arts called San Francisco Psychedelic. One whole room was posters from the Avalon and the Fillmore - a lot for the eyes to process! Nice setup. I''m not sure I''m crazy about the border here but I suppose it fits in quite well. (Not voting, just passing through. :) )', '2007-03-30 14:05:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(3499804, 488075, 66635, '<td valign="top">People died because of these cartoons.  If the censors in the country where I live see this, they''ll block access to DPChallenge.  Rule 4.2 of the Terms of Service prohibits pictures that do "or may" denigrate religion.  Given the strength of Muslim feelings over these images, I''m disheartened that the Site Council has chosen to ignore its own rule and allow the picture to stand (thereby leaving the rest of us members in confusion as to what the actual rules on freedom of speech and censorship in 4.2 actually are).  Please note that I strongly disagree with the Muslim reaction to these cartoons; but the reaction is what it is and Rule 4.2 supposedly exists to respect that.  <br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-04-02 04:34:12.</i></td>', 'People died because of these cartoons.  If the censors in the country where I live see this, they''ll block access to DPChallenge.  Rule 4.2 of the Terms of Service prohibits pictures that do "or may" denigrate religion.  Given the strength of Muslim feelings over these images, I''m disheartened that the Site Council has chosen to ignore its own rule and allow the picture to stand (thereby leaving the rest of us members in confusion as to what the actual rules on freedom of speech and censorship in 4.2 actually are).  Please note that I strongly disagree with the Muslim reaction to these cartoons; but the reaction is what it is and Rule 4.2 supposedly exists to respect that.  ', '2007-03-30 14:16:22.000000', '2007-04-02 05:34:12.000000', 1),
